## Core Development Guidelines

- Strict typing in GDScript
- Call `super()` lifecycle methods only when the parent class defines them
- Use `@onready` for node references
- Prefer composition over inheritance; use signals for loose coupling
- Nodes: PascalCase; methods: snake_case

## Swappable Systems (Strategy Pattern)

- **Contract** = `@abstract class_name` base with `@abstract func`s (compile-time enforcement)
- **Strategy** = concrete `Resource` subclass as `.tres`; inject via `@export`, swap by assigning a different file
- **Config** = `Resource` (`.tres`) of `@export` tuning values; new archetypes → new `.tres`, not duplicated scripts
- Keep strategies stateless — pass body/intent/config in, return results
- Transient cross-system data = `RefCounted` objects, not cross-node reaches
- Promote to component Node / `@export PackedScene` only when needing `_physics_process`, collision, or signals
- Reusable systems live in `libs/` (no `src/` references); `src/<slice>/` composes them

## Code Style

- Type hints on all variables and parameters
- Docstrings on complex functions; keep methods focused and comments minimal
- Group related properties and methods
- Keep comments as succinct as possible

## Naming Conventions

- Files, variables, functions: snake_case
- Classes, enum types, nodes: PascalCase
- Constants, enum values: ALL_CAPS_SNAKE_CASE
- Signals: snake_case, past tense (e.g. `health_depleted`)
- Variables: specific and readable — avoid vague names (`data`, `temp`, `val`) and single letters outside loops/math; add domain or unit when needed (`movement_speed_px_per_s`, `is_on_floor`)

## Scenes

- Minimize scene tree depth; use inheritance for reusable components
- Clean up on `queue_free()`; use SubViewports sparingly
- Give step-by-step scene creation instructions instead of pasting `.tscn` source

## Signals

- Typed signals with clear, contextual names
- Connect in code for dynamic nodes, editor for static
- Reserve for important events; pass minimal args (avoid whole node refs)
- Disconnect on free; use EventBus autoload for global events

## Resources & Performance

- `preload()` essential, `load()` optional; clean up in `_exit_tree()`
- Prefer direct node refs over groups for hot paths; use physics layers; prefer packed arrays

## Error Handling

- Graceful fallbacks for missing resources; `assert()` in dev

## 2D

- Build on `Node2D` trees — `Sprite2D`, `AnimatedSprite2D`, `TileMapLayer`, `Camera2D`
- Physics: `CharacterBody2D`, `RigidBody2D`, `Area2D` with `CollisionShape2D` / `CollisionPolygon2D`
- Do not introduce 3D nodes (`Node3D`, `MeshInstance3D`, `Camera3D`, etc.) unless explicitly requested
- Prefer `CanvasLayer` for HUD; keep gameplay under a `Node2D` root with `Camera2D`

## TileMap

- Use `TileMapLayer` nodes (TileMap is deprecated); access 2D navigation via `TileMapLayer.get_navigation_map()`
